# Static Pod Demo

This folder shows how a pod can be run as a static pod in the `kube-system` namespace.

## What it does

The manifest is meant to be placed in the static pod directory on a node, usually `/etc/kubernetes/manifests`.

Kubernetes watches that directory and launches the pod automatically without using the usual API-based deployment workflow.

## Example purpose

- run control-plane or node-level services
- demonstrate static pod behavior
- show how kubelet reads manifests from a configured directory
